# `openapi.json` and `src/lib/api/schema.ts` are generated by
# `pnpm generate:api` — and they ARE checked in. They used to be ignored here,
# on the reasoning that a stale copy could not drift if it was never committed.
# The cost was worse than the risk: `src/lib/api/types.ts` imports the
# generated schema, so a fresh clone could not type-check or build at all until
# someone stood up a Python virtualenv and ran the backend. The frontend is not
# meant to need one.
#
# Staleness is now caught rather than avoided:
# `backend/tests/contract/test_openapi_artifact_is_current.py` regenerates the
# document and fails if the committed copy differs, so a backend route change
# that skips `pnpm generate:api` breaks the build instead of silently shipping
# a frontend typed against an API that no longer exists.

*.log
